    "https://www.cornerstone.edu/about/employment/": {
      "title": "Office of People and Culture",
      "description": "Office of People & Culture | Cornerstone University About Us Athletics Alumni Wisdom Conversations Give 616.949.5300 Visit Campus Apply Cornerstone University Academics Admissions Online Student Life Tuition & Aid 616.949.5300 Search All Programs Associate Degrees Bachelor’s Degrees Master’s Degrees Doctoral Degree Online Degrees Certificates Minors Schools & Seminary First Year Online Graduate SOAR™ Mobile Transfer Dual Enrollment International Students Apply Net Price Calculator Military & Veteran Benefits Apply for Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans On-Campus Experience Online Experience Seminary Experience Career Services Student Services & Resources Online Admissions Online Degrees SOAR™ Mobile Degrees Online Experience Center for Academic Success Office of People and Culture Cornerstone University is a dynamic Christian community that is building upon a strong foundation for an even brighter future for students, alumni, faculty and staff. Every employee plays a vital role in shaping a successful future for the University. We seek individuals who are passionate about their relationship with Jesus Christ, their continued growth as a professional and their care for each other and our community. View Job Openings The Cornerstone University Culture Benefits Summary Student Employment Information Information on how to find jobs on campus Login to your Handshake account Click on “Jobs” Click on “Cornerstone Collections” and choose “on campus jobs” Instructions for onboarding Required Employment Paperwork Before your first day of employment, you must schedule an appointment with the Office of People and Culture to complete your Form I‑9 and tax forms (W‑4, MI‑W‑4, and CF‑W‑4). These forms are required to comply with federal and state regulations and are necessary for you to receive pay. Links to the required forms are provided below. Scheduling Your Appointment To set up an appointment with the Office of People and Culture, login to your Handshake account and navigate to the Career Center. Then, click on appointments and schedule a new appointment. Choose the “student employment” category and choose a time and date that works best for your schedule prior to your first day of employment. Identification Requirements for Your Appointment: For your scheduled appointment, you must present a valid form of identification. Acceptable documents include: A valid passport, or A driver’s license combined with a Social Security card A certified birth certificate may be used in place of a Social Security card All documents must be original or certified copies. Photocopies, digital images, or photographs of documents will not be accepted. For further instructions, please see page 2 of Form I-9. 2026 Student Employee Hiring Forms (PDF) Details surrounding policies of student employment Student employee positions are classified into two levels based on expected weekly hours: Level 1 Positions: Roles that typically require 12–20 hours per week, with a maximum of 20 hours per week. Level 2 Positions: Roles that typically require fewer than 10 hours per week. Regardless of position level, students may not work more than 20 total hours per week during the academic term. Students may hold multiple positions only in the following approved combinations: One Level 1 position and one Level 2 position Two Level 2 positions Any modified Level 1 job combinations require prior approval from the Office of People and Culture . 1095C Tax Form Distribution Notice Notification for current and former employees covered on the university health plans for some or all of 2025. Due to new federal legislation designed to reduce paperwork and administrative burden, we are informing you of upcoming changes to how Form 1095-C will be distributed. Previously, we were required to automatically provide you with Form 1095-C each year. However, due to recent changes in federal law, we are now only required to furnish this form to you upon request. What is Form 1095-C? Form 1095-C provides information about the health insurance coverage we offered you during the year. You are not required to file this statement with your personal taxes. How to Request Your Form 1095-C: If you would like to receive Form 1095-C for the 2025 tax year, you can request the form by: Emailing us at OPC@Cornerstone.edu Calling us at 616-254-1640 Writing us at Office of People & Culture, Cornerstone University, 1001 E. Beltline Ave NE, Grand Rapids, MI 49525 Cornerstone University will provide your Form 1095-C within 30 days of your request. We appreciate your understanding and cooperation. If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact us. 2026 Payroll Calendars 2026 Payroll Calendar for Hourly Employees (PDF) 2026 Payroll Calendar for Salaried Employees (PDF) Cornerstone University Contact P: 616.949.5300 E: info@cornerstone.edu Address 1001 East Beltline Ave NE Grand Rapids , MI 49525 Hours MON - FRI: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. SAT & SUN: Closed Plan a Visit Apply Want To Learn More About CU? Request Info Apply Today Connect With CU Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Cornerstone University Get In Touch 1001 East Beltline Avenue NE Grand Rapids, MI 49525 616.949.5300 CONTACT US Helpful Links Accreditation Faculty Directory Maps & Directions Library Current Students Careers at CU Facility Virtual Tour University Offices Title IX Privacy Policy Campus Store 91.3 WCSG Academic Catalog Events Cornerstone University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. © 2026 Cornerstone University. All Rights Reserved. About Us Academic Programs All Programs Associate Degrees Bachelor’s Degrees Master’s Degrees Doctoral Degrees Online Degrees SOAR™ Mobile Degrees Certificates Minors Schools & Seminary Admissions View All Admissions First Year Online Graduate SOAR™ Mobile Transfer Dual Enrollment International Students Apply Student Experience Overview Campus Experience Online Experience Seminary Experience Career Services Resources Tuition + Financial Aid Overview Net Price Calculator Military & Veteran Benefits Apply For Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans Alumni Athletics Contact Us Events Apply Today Current Students Give to Cornerstone Submit Close Search Suggested Academics Admissions Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Common About Cornerstone University Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Give to CU Recent News Cornerstone University Extends Tuition Freeze for Fall 2026–27, 2nd Consecutive Year New Wisdom & Influence Podcast Debut from Cornerstone University Cornerstone Enrollment Rises With Career-ready, Christian Worldview Focus"
    },
    "https://www.cornerstone.edu/university-offices/career-services/": {
      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services | Cornerstone University About Us Athletics Alumni Wisdom Conversations Give 616.949.5300 Visit Campus Apply Cornerstone University Academics Admissions Online Student Life Tuition & Aid 616.949.5300 Search All Programs Associate Degrees Bachelor’s Degrees Master’s Degrees Doctoral Degree Online Degrees Certificates Minors Schools & Seminary First Year Online Graduate SOAR™ Mobile Transfer Dual Enrollment International Students Apply Net Price Calculator Military & Veteran Benefits Apply for Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans On-Campus Experience Online Experience Seminary Experience Career Services Student Services & Resources Online Admissions Online Degrees SOAR™ Mobile Degrees Online Experience Center for Academic Success Office of Career and Life Calling Career Services University Offices Students Employers Alumni Parents Please Select Students Employers Alumni Parents Welcome to Career and Life Calling’s Career Services! Here, students find support, direction, and confidence as they pursue God’s calling and prepare for meaningful careers. Guided by the Cornerstone Advantage™, we help students grow as morally grounded, career-ready leaders through personalized coaching, practical tools, and opportunities for real-world experience. Our Services Personalized career and calling coaching Major and career exploration resources Résumé, cover letter, interview prep and Internship search support Graduate school planning and application assistance Access to Handshake and career development tools Employer job and internship postings/campus recruitment Career Exploration Resume & Interviews Who’s Hiring On Campus Jobs & Internships Employers Handshake The Cornerstone Advantage™: Readying You for Life, Career & Influence Moral Goodness Academic Expertise Experiential Learning Leadership Learning Talent Acceleration This meeting gave me more confidence and a more open mind about my future career. —Colin H. It gave me clarity about how to approach the future and confidence that I’m heading the in the right direction. —Kyler N. I left the meeting feeling like I had a clearer direction and a plan for how to intentionally develop my skills moving forward. —Coby F. I left that conversation very encouraged and excited to see what the Lord has in store for me. —Carson K. Cornerstone University Contact P: 616.949.5300 E: info@cornerstone.edu Address 1001 East Beltline Ave NE Grand Rapids , MI 49525 Hours MON - FRI: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. SAT & SUN: Closed Plan a Visit Apply Want To Learn More About CU? Request Info Apply Today Connect With CU Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Cornerstone University Get In Touch 1001 East Beltline Avenue NE Grand Rapids, MI 49525 616.949.5300 CONTACT US Helpful Links Accreditation Faculty Directory Maps & Directions Library Current Students Careers at CU Facility Virtual Tour University Offices Title IX Privacy Policy Campus Store 91.3 WCSG Academic Catalog Events Cornerstone University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. © 2026 Cornerstone University. All Rights Reserved. About Us Academic Programs All Programs Associate Degrees Bachelor’s Degrees Master’s Degrees Doctoral Degrees Online Degrees SOAR™ Mobile Degrees Certificates Minors Schools & Seminary Admissions View All Admissions First Year Online Graduate SOAR™ Mobile Transfer Dual Enrollment International Students Apply Student Experience Overview Campus Experience Online Experience Seminary Experience Career Services Resources Tuition + Financial Aid Overview Net Price Calculator Military & Veteran Benefits Apply For Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans Alumni Athletics Contact Us Events Apply Today Current Students Give to Cornerstone Submit Close Search Suggested Academics Admissions Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Common About Cornerstone University Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Give to CU Recent News Cornerstone University Extends Tuition Freeze for Fall 2026–27, 2nd Consecutive Year New Wisdom & Influence Podcast Debut from Cornerstone University Cornerstone Enrollment Rises With Career-ready, Christian Worldview Focus"
    },
    "https://www.cornerstone.edu/cornerstone-enrollment-rises-with-career-ready-christian-worldview-focus/": {
      "title": "Cornerstone University Growth With Career-Ready Christian Focus",
      "description": "Enrollment Rises with Career-Ready Focus | Cornerstone University About Us Athletics Alumni Wisdom Conversations Give 616.949.5300 Visit Campus Apply Cornerstone University Academics Admissions Online Student Life Tuition & Aid 616.949.5300 Search All Programs Associate Degrees Bachelor’s Degrees Master’s Degrees Doctoral Degree Online Degrees Certificates Minors Schools & Seminary First Year Online Graduate SOAR™ Mobile Transfer Dual Enrollment International Students Apply Net Price Calculator Military & Veteran Benefits Apply for Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans On-Campus Experience Online Experience Seminary Experience Career Services Student Services & Resources Online Admissions Online Degrees SOAR™ Mobile Degrees Online Experience Center for Academic Success Cornerstone University Growth With Career-Ready Christian Focus News September 2, 2025 Cornerstone University is celebrating strong enrollment increases for fall 2025, with a total enrollment increase of 11% over last year. The growth reflects the university’s commitment to career-ready programs that are affordable and distinctly guided by a Christian worldview that prepares graduates to positively influence industries and communities. The numbers underscore the university’s broad appeal: new freshmen and transfer student enrollment increased by 18% year over year, while the online population grew 6%. An additional driver of growth is SOAR™ , the university’s first-in-the-nation smartphone-based app featuring an innovative business management bachelor’s degree. “Students and families are choosing Cornerstone because they see the value of what we call The Cornerstone Advantage™ ,” said President Gerson Moreno-Riaño . “By integrating moral formation, market-aligned skills, leadership and talent development, and experiential learning, we prepare students for a meaningful career and flourishing life. This fall’s increase shows that this vision is resonating in powerful ways.” Other contributing factors to the fall increases included: 22% undergraduate tuition reset in 2024. Tuition freeze for 2025 and 2026. Online tuition held flat for five years at the lowest rate in the region. Enhanced career support services. “Cornerstone is grateful students are responding to the steps we’ve taken to make our Christ-centered education more accessible and valuable,” said Heidi Cece, executive vice president for enrollment management and marketing. “We’ve focused on affordability, added and refined in-demand programs that match market needs, and emphasized the skills employers want. Combined with a vibrant campus life and expanded access online and through our mobile-delivered SOAR™ program, Cornerstone is delivering the experience students are seeking.” From traditional college students to online adult learners to workers seeking upskilling programs, Cornerstone serves students at every stage and is one of the most affordable, accredited private universities in Michigan, the Midwest, and the rest of the nation. Cornerstone University invites you to explore our 65 on-campus and online degree programs and SOAR™ mobile app business management degree by contacting admissions@cornerstone.edu . Share Related News View All News September 4, 2026 Convocation 2026: Living Ready for Jesus Christ to Return View News September 3, 2026 Christ & Culture Week: Biblical Truth and Today’s Culture View News September 2, 2026 Record Attendance at First Chapel as President Moreno-Riaño Challenges Cornerstone: “Are You Ready?” View News August 18, 2026 Strikes for Stripes 2026: Celebrate America at 250 and Honor America’s West Michigan Heroes View Sept.  15, 2026 A Documentary Screening and Q&A With Ryan Bomberger View Sept.  11, 2026 9/11 Memorial Chapel Feat. Eric Metaxas View Sept.  10, 2026 Eric Metaxas Presents “Revolution”: Book Talk & Signing View News August 12, 2026 “The AI Literacy Test Higher Education Must Not Fail” Op-Ed Featured in Washington Examiner View Want to Learn More About CU? Request Info Apply Today Connect With CU Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Cornerstone University Get In Touch 1001 East Beltline Avenue NE Grand Rapids, MI 49525 616.949.5300 CONTACT US Helpful Links Accreditation Faculty Directory Maps & Directions Library Current Students Careers at CU Facility Virtual Tour University Offices Title IX Privacy Policy Campus Store 91.3 WCSG Academic Catalog Events Cornerstone University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. © 2026 Cornerstone University. All Rights Reserved. About Us Academic Programs All Programs Associate Degrees Bachelor’s Degrees Master’s Degrees Doctoral Degrees Online Degrees SOAR™ Mobile Degrees Certificates Minors Schools & Seminary Admissions View All Admissions First Year Online Graduate SOAR™ Mobile Transfer Dual Enrollment International Students Apply Student Experience Overview Campus Experience Online Experience Seminary Experience Career Services Resources Tuition + Financial Aid Overview Net Price Calculator Military & Veteran Benefits Apply For Aid Scholarships & Grants Loans Alumni Athletics Contact Us Events Apply Today Current Students Give to Cornerstone Submit Close Search Suggested Academics Admissions Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Common About Cornerstone University Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Give to CU Recent News Cornerstone University Extends Tuition Freeze for Fall 2026–27, 2nd Consecutive Year New Wisdom & Influence Podcast Debut from Cornerstone University Cornerstone Enrollment Rises With Career-ready, Christian Worldview Focus"
    }
